<header class="g hero">
  <div class="side lab mut">03 / 08</div>
  <div class="main">
    <h1>Praktika.school</h1>
    <p class="lead">A mobile app for an online school that helps students stick with their studies</p>
    <div class="meta">
      <div><span class="lab mut">Role</span>UI/UX designer</div>
      <div><span class="lab mut">Year</span>2024</div>
      <div><span class="lab mut">Tools</span>Figma</div>
      <div><span class="lab mut">Platform</span>iOS</div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="full cover"><div class="pk"><img src="/img/praktika/cover.jpg" alt="Praktika.school"></div></div>
</header>

<div class="g body">
  <aside class="side toc" data-native><span class="lab mut">Contents</span><ol id="toc"></ol><div class="prog"><i id="prog"></i></div><a href="/en/" class="all lab mut">← all work</a></aside>
  <main class="main" id="main" data-native>

  <section class="ch" id="about" data-t="About the project">
    <div class="ch-h"><h2><span class="n">01</span>About the project</h2><p>An online school with courses in design, advertising, marketing and sales.</p></div>
    <p class="txt big">Praktika.school is an educational platform with lectures and courses. Students study alongside their jobs, and they’re easy to lose: they forget about a lesson, miss a deadline, disappear.</p>
    <dl class="kv"><dt class="lab">Goal</dt><dd>Design a modern, easy-to-use mobile app that helps increase student engagement.</dd>
      <dt class="lab">Stages</dt><dd>Competitive analysis → audience interviews → User and Job Stories → User Flow → wireframes → UI kit → prototype.</dd></dl>
  </section>

  <section class="ch" id="research" data-t="Research">
    <div class="ch-h"><h2><span class="n">02</span>Research</h2><p>Three online school apps, references and three in-depth interviews.</p></div>
    <dl class="kv" style="margin-top:0"><dt class="lab">Competitors</dt><dd>Stepik, “Pravoe polusharie introverta” (“The Introvert’s Right Hemisphere”) and Kontur School: what they do well, where they go wrong and what can be reused. It surprised me that some popular schools, such as Contented and Skillbox, have no app at all.</dd>
      <dt class="lab">References</dt><dd>Screens from Dribbble, Behance and the Figma community — sign-in, catalog, course card, player, profile. The visual style comes from the school’s website: acid green, black outlines, stars and lines.</dd>
      <dt class="lab">Audience</dt><dd>People aged 25 to 44 with average incomes who want to change careers or level up their skills. They study in the evening, on their phones, between work and errands.</dd>
      <dt class="lab">Interviews</dt><dd>Three participants, Zoom, 25–⁠50&nbsp;minutes. R1 is changing careers, R2 is building skills in their own field, R3 is moving into an adjacent one. Their learning experience ranges from big online schools to small author-led courses.</dd></dl>
    <h3>What I learned from the interviews</h3>
    <div class="hyps">
      <div class="hyp"><span class="n lab mut">01</span><p>People want an app to study on the go and keep track of feedback, webinars and deadlines</p><span class="r"><span class="lab mut">R1, R2</span></span></div>
      <div class="hyp"><span class="n lab mut">02</span><p>Communication drifts off to Slack, Discord and work chats — they want it inside the platform</p><span class="r"><span class="lab mut">R1, R3</span></span></div>
      <div class="hyp"><span class="n lab mut">03</span><p>Video alone isn’t enough: they need a summary, timestamped notes and comments tied to a moment in the lecture</p><span class="r"><span class="lab mut">R1, R3</span></span></div>
      <div class="hyp"><span class="n lab mut">04</span><p>Whether deadlines help depends on the format: for career changers they help beat procrastination, in lectures taken “just for yourself” they get in the way</p><span class="r"><span class="lab mut">R1, R2, R3</span></span></div>
      <div class="hyp"><span class="n lab mut">05</span><p>They want to see course progress and the subscription balance, and to cancel without calling a manager</p><span class="r"><span class="lab mut">R1, R2</span></span></div>
      <div class="hyp"><span class="n lab mut">06</span><p>Several sign-in options are needed: text messages don’t arrive, and social login is hidden</p><span class="r"><span class="lab mut">R2</span></span></div>
    </div>
    <h3>User Stories and Job Stories</h3>
    <div class="stories">
      <div><span class="lab mut">User Stories</span>
        <q>As a student, I want to see a progress indicator in my account so I can plan my weekly workload realistically and stay motivated.</q>
        <q>As a student, I want to filter courses by price and field so I only spend time on learning that matches my goals.</q>
        <q>As a student, I want to always see my account balance so I can keep track of my payment schedule and not interrupt my studies.</q>
        <q>As a student, I want to sign in with social media so I spend my time studying, not recovering my password.</q></div>
      <div><span class="lab mut">Job Stories</span>
        <q>When I’m watching a lecture, I want to make notes in one click so I can come back to the key points when I practice without rewatching the whole video.</q>
        <q>When my head is full of work tasks, I want to get reminders about my studies so I don’t miss anything and finish the course.</q>
        <q>When I’m watching a lecture on my phone in bed, I want to quickly ask the teacher a question so I don’t forget it and apply the knowledge correctly.</q>
        <q>When things are on fire at work, I want to move a project deadline within the allowed limits so I can hand in quality work without sacrificing the rest of my life.</q></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="ch" id="flow" data-t="Structure">
    <div class="ch-h"><h2><span class="n">03</span>Structure</h2><p>Five sections in the bottom menu and a short path from sign-in to a lesson.</p></div>
    <div class="flowmap">
      <div class="col"><b>Home</b><ul><li>In progress</li><li>Favorites</li><li>Downloaded</li><li>Completed</li><li class="sub">Certificates</li></ul></div>
      <div class="col"><b>Courses</b><ul><li>Filters</li><li>Search</li><li>Course page</li><li class="sub">Lesson player</li><li class="sub">Assignment</li></ul></div>
      <div class="col"><b>Lectures</b><ul><li>Filters</li><li>Search</li><li class="sub">Continue</li></ul></div>
      <div class="col"><b>Chats</b><ul><li>Curator</li><li>Mentor</li><li>Group</li></ul></div>
      <div class="col"><b>Profile</b><ul><li>Subscription</li><li class="sub">Renew, cancel</li><li>Activity</li><li>Settings</li><li class="sub">Theme, language, notifications</li></ul></div>
    </div>
    <div class="entry"><span>Sign-in</span>→<span>Home</span>→<span>Course in progress</span>→<span>Course page</span>→<span>Lesson player</span>→<span>Assignment</span></div>
  </section>

  <section class="ch" id="wireframes" data-t="Wireframes">
    <div class="ch-h"><h2><span class="n">04</span>Wireframes</h2><p>First, the screen structure in gray, with no color or illustrations. Every decision comes from the interviews or the competitor review.</p></div>
    <div class="wfgrid" id="wfgrid"></div>
  </section>

  <section class="ch" id="system" data-t="Design system">
    <div class="ch-h"><h2><span class="n">05</span>Design system</h2><p>Dark navigation, two bright accents and 3D illustrations.</p></div>
    <div class="pk-type"><div class="aa">Aa</div><div class="rt"><div class="abc">Montserrat<br>Aa Bb Cc Dd Ee Ff Gg Hh Ii Jj Kk Ll Mm Nn Oo Pp Qq Rr Ss Tt Uu Vv Ww Xx Yy Zz</div>
      <div class="sizes"><span style="font-size:12px">12&nbsp;pt</span><span style="font-size:14px">14&nbsp;pt</span><span style="font-size:18px">18&nbsp;pt</span><span style="font-size:24px">24&nbsp;pt</span></div></div></div>
    <div class="sw" style="grid-template-columns:2fr 2fr 1fr 1fr 1fr 1fr">
      <div style="background:#f0d8fb">Lavender<small>accent, secondary buttons</small></div>
      <div style="background:#ebfe8b">Lime<small>accent, active state</small></div>
      <div style="background:#151b15;color:#fff">Dark<small>menu, buttons</small></div>
      <div style="background:#777;color:#fff">Gray<small>inactive</small></div>
      <div style="background:#e3e3e3">Lines</div>
      <div style="background:#fff;box-shadow:inset 0 0 0 1px #e8e6e1">Background</div>
    </div>
    <div class="pk-pills"><span style="background:#ebfe8b">Continue learning</span><span style="background:#f0d8fb">Lecture summary</span><span style="background:#151b15;color:#fff">Sign in</span><span style="background:#777;color:#fff;border-color:#777">Disabled</span><span class="r" style="background:#ebfe8b">Watch</span><span class="r">UI/UX</span><span class="r">4.9</span></div>
    <figure class="f"><img src="/img/praktika/illus.png" alt="" style="width:100%;display:block"><figcaption class="lab mut">Illustrations for course and lecture covers</figcaption></figure>
  </section>

  <section class="ch" id="screens" data-t="Screens">
    <div class="ch-h"><h2><span class="n">06</span>Screens</h2><p>Nine screens, from sign-in to certificate.</p></div>
    <div class="screens">
      <figure><img src="/img/praktika/s-login.jpg" alt=""><figcaption><span class="lab mut">Sign-in</span>Email, phone or social media — no extra passwords</figcaption></figure>
      <figure><img src="/img/praktika/s-home-courses.jpg" alt=""><figcaption><span class="lab mut">Home</span>My courses and progress on each one</figcaption></figure>
      <figure><img src="/img/praktika/s-home-lect.jpg" alt=""><figcaption><span class="lab mut">Home</span>Lectures: in progress, favorites, completed</figcaption></figure>
      <figure><img src="/img/praktika/s-course.jpg" alt=""><figcaption><span class="lab mut">Course</span>Description, learning stats, list of lessons</figcaption></figure>
      <figure><img src="/img/praktika/s-player.jpg" alt=""><figcaption><span class="lab mut">Lesson</span>Player, summary, notes and homework</figcaption></figure>
      <figure><img src="/img/praktika/s-catalog.jpg" alt=""><figcaption><span class="lab mut">Lectures</span>Catalog with search and filters</figcaption></figure>
      <figure><img src="/img/praktika/s-account.jpg" alt=""><figcaption><span class="lab mut">Profile</span>Subscription and activity calendar</figcaption></figure>
      <figure><img src="/img/praktika/s-cert.jpg" alt=""><figcaption><span class="lab mut">Certificate</span>The course result, ready to download</figcaption></figure>
      <figure><img src="/img/praktika/s-chats.jpg" alt=""><figcaption><span class="lab mut">Chats</span>Curator, mentor and group</figcaption></figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="ch" id="testing" data-t="Testing">
    <div class="ch-h"><h2><span class="n">07</span>Testing</h2><p>A usability test of the prototype with two respondents: the main scenario and 13 additional tasks.</p></div>
    <p class="txt">The main task: “Continue the ‘Web Design in Figma’ course.” The additional ones: find favorites, completed courses and the certificate, the catalog with filters, chats, language settings and subscription renewal.</p>
    <dl class="kv"><dt class="lab">What worked</dt><dd>Both participants got through the additional scenarios with no trouble. R2 first explored the home screen and then completed every task without mistakes.</dd>
      <dt class="lab">Where they stumbled</dt><dd>R1 looked for a purchased course in the “Courses” catalog instead of on Home, and for favorites in “Profile.” Both kept missing small buttons.</dd>
      <dt class="lab">What to fix</dt><dd>Add “My courses” and “My lectures” tabs to “Courses” and “Lectures” that lead to Home, and make tap areas larger. For a new user, Home is empty until they buy something, so the mix-up with the catalog is understandable.</dd></dl>
  </section>

  <section class="ch" id="result" data-t="Results">
    <div class="ch-h"><h2><span class="n">08</span>Results</h2><p>A study project: from research to a prototype and a usability test.</p></div>
    <dl class="kv" style="margin-top:0"><dt class="lab">What was done</dt><dd>Competitor review, three interviews, User and Job Stories, structure and user flows, wireframes, UI kit, prototype and a test with two respondents.</dd>
      <dt class="lab">Progress</dt><dd>Learning stats and a percentage for each course — you can see how much is left.</dd>
      <dt class="lab">Learning in short bursts</dt><dd>Offline downloads, “continue” from where you left off, notes and a summary right in the player.</dd>
      <dt class="lab">Staying in touch</dt><dd>Chats with the curator, mentor and group, so no question gets lost.</dd>
      <dt class="lab">Motivation</dt><dd>An activity calendar in the profile and a certificate at the end of the course.</dd></dl>
  </section>
  </main>
</div>

